\newlabel{sec:results_fpr}{{\mbox  {VI-D}}{6}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces False Positive Rate (FPR) vs. Market Volatility. As the volatility multiplier $\gamma $ increases from $1\times $ to $5\times $, the baseline model's FPR grows to 7.1\%, while the proposed AEWMA approach maintains near-zero FPR (0.4\% at $5\times $) due to the adaptive $\alpha _t$ dampening mechanism.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fpr}{{3}{6}}
